<title>USA: Shiva Q1 hurt by price competition, charge.</title>
<headline>Shiva Q1 hurt by price competition, charge.</headline>
<dateline>BEDFORD, Mass. 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shiva Corp said on Thursday that its first quarter results were hurt by price competition for its Lan Rover products and a charges totaling $0.28 a share for write-downs and price protection costs.</p>
<p>The company increased its price protection reserves in the quarter, which hurt revenues by $6.7 million, Shiva said.</p>
<p>The reserve was taken in anticipation of price reductions on certain products planned for the second quarter, Shiva said.</p>
